{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457145-discipline-activaton-during-dramatic-scenes-pre-5th","id":1457145,"title":"Discipline activaton during dramatic scenes pre 5th","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-18T15:04:09-07:00","id":1457145,"title":"Discipline activaton during dramatic scenes pre 5th","content":"When do disciplines like form of mist or vanish from minds eye happen during combat; when I activate or at end of turn?<br /> When celerity or claws of the dead?<br /> If I can turn to mist on declaration its only necessary to win Initiative to be safe from a lot of threats.<br /> As a storteller is it OK to say transformation is fully established at turns end?<br /> But to say discipline effects happen on beginning of next turn would be problematic with the other disciplines named above...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T20:40:41-07:00","id":1457173,"title":"","content":"Pre 5th initiative rules are messy, but it never had the concept of &quot;effect at X point on round&quot;. In theory it always happens at the moment you activate, but as ST it is ok for you to assume that fully transformation doesn't takes hold immediately.<br /> <br /> But this is less of a problem than you seem to think. Those powers aren't necessarily balanced, but are intended to work that way and it won't harm your game as much. Specially, the ability of getting out of combat isn't nearly as game-breaking as damage already is, thanks to the damage penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T00:24:33-07:00","id":1457189,"title":"","content":"Well its an elder game.<br /> The characters have lots of disciplines.<br /> Damage was not a problem for me.<br /> But the ability to vanish in an instant, without having eg celerity vampires a chance even did bother me.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T11:21:30-07:00","id":1457218,"title":"","content":"I would just say the Discipline activates on your turn, not during the declaration phase. Anyone acting after you can't hit you. But Celerity should increase Initiative too, so that Celerity vamp may get the drop on the vanishing PC anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-19T13:07:32-07:00","id":1457226,"title":"","content":"Virtually all 1-5 protean requires a minimum of a turn to activate.<br /> Presence is instant, except those that require a roll, which are done on your turn. <br /> Celerity is declared then goes at the end of a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-20-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T16:16:45-07:00","id":1457523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457145-discipline-activaton-during-dramatic-scenes-pre-5th?p=1457189#post1457189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its an elder game.<br /> The characters have lots of disciplines.<br /> Damage was not a problem for me.<br /> But the ability to vanish in an instant, without having eg celerity vampires a chance even did bother me.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where are the characters going? I think you're tackling the problem from the wrong perspective.<br /> <br /> The character that takes Form of Mist is mostly invulnerable, but is mostly incapable of interacting, too, specially if their goal is to flee. This is a major weakness by itself, since they're unable to properly oppose their assailants in doing whatever else they're doing.<br /> <br /> Instead of banging your head against how to stop players (or NPCs) from fleeing, start having their opponents capitalize the moment to act unhindered. A vampire still needs a place to sleep through the day, blood (specially to fuel those Discipline uses), and other resources (including Resources). They live in the setting and have reasons to be in that combat in the first place, if things went south and they're fleeing, then they already lost the battle and its spoils.<br /> <br /> Even action-packed, combat-oriented stories should work fine with instant Mist Form. D&amp;D does so, by the way, and it is just as reliable as a defense. Think less about how easy it makes for the characters to flee and more on why fleeing are working so well as a strategy. It shouldn't, and maybe isn't.<br /> <br /> And in the end of the day, nothing at all stops you from making the transformation take hold later in the round, not even RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}